      {
        "heading": "The short version",
        "text": "Logan Michael Evans (born June 5, 2001) is an American professional baseball pitcher for the Seattle Mariners of Major League Baseball (MLB). He made his MLB debut in 2025."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Lately",
        "text": "Evans was assigned to the Triple-A Tacoma Rainiers to begin the 2025 season, posting a 3.86 ERA with 23 strikeouts over five starts. On April 27, Evans was selected to the 40-man roster and promoted to the major leagues for the first time. In his debut that afternoon against the Miami Marlins, Evans earned the win, tossing five innings and allowing two runs with three strikeouts. He made 16 appearances (15 starts) for Seattle during his rookie season, with a 6–5 record, 4.32 ERA, and 59 strikeouts across 81+1⁄3 innings pitched."
      }
